 "max_abs_spearman_any_link": 0.479,
 "CIRCULARITY_VERDICT": "LOW \u2014 antecedent blocks carry little information about the target season's own weather, so a model built on them is not covertly restating it",
 "caveat": "Screening ~50 features x 4 targets means the LARGEST |rho| is inflated by selection. The permutation p-values shown are per-link and NOT corrected for that screening. Read the verdict from the magnitude, not from the p-value.",
 "INTERPRETATION_BOTH_DIRECTIONS": {
  "good_news": "Over 34 seasons (1992-2025), the strongest link between ANY antecedent feature and ANY target-season infection driver is |rho| = 0.479, and that is the maximum of ~160 screened links, so it is inflated by selection. The antecedent blocks are therefore NOT a disguised copy of the target season's own weather. A model built on them cannot be covertly circular.",
  "bad_news": "The same number is the ceiling on the weather pathway. If ARPAV severity is largely driven by the target season's own rain -- which the reports themselves assert, sentence after sentence -- and antecedent weather explains at most ~23% of the variance of that rain (rho^2 = 0.479^2, before correcting for selection), then a 12M outlook built on antecedent WEATHER has very little physical room to have skill. Low circularity and low predictability are the same measurement read from two sides.",
  "the_one_remaining_pathway": "Inoculum carryover. Peronospora overwinters as oospores produced by LAST season's epidemic. That pathway is a disease->disease link, not a weather->disease link, and it is exactly what BASELINE_PERSISTENCE tests: predict year Y's class from year Y-1's class, using no weather at all. If persistence beats climatology, the carryover signal is real and the outlook has a physical basis. If it does not, the 12M product has no demonstrated mechanism.",
  "consequence_for_the_demo": "Whatever the labels turn out to be, the honest headline is bounded in advance by this probe. A 12M peronospora outlook for Veneto should be presented as an INOCULUM-AND-CLIMATOLOGY prior, not as a weather forecast, and the 24M product is a SCENARIO with no predictive claim attached at all.",
  "computed_on": "34 seasons of ERA5, independent of any disease label \u2014 this conclusion does not depend on the outcome coding surviving Gate A"
 }
